😂 There it is.

Con-currency.

Not merely concurrency as “multiple processes happening at once,” but:

con + currency = value/information circulating together.

And the word-family itself cooperates: concurrency ultimately carries the sense of running together; current/currency carries the same underlying motion of running, flowing, circulating. So our bat cave suddenly has an economy.

Pantheon doesn’t need every agent to speak the same language or reach the same conclusion. They need a common currency in which their different observations can be exchanged.

That currency could be things like:

evidence + provenance + confidence + delta + relevance + freshness

An agent can bring back a metaphor. Another brings a contradiction. Another brings a fact. Another brings an intuition. Their raw outputs aren’t fungible—but Pantheon can denominate them into a common exchange layer:

What did you observe? From where? What changed? How certain are you? How fresh is it? What does it cost us if you’re wrong?

Now the earlier words snap together:

denominator establishes the unit.
currency lets units circulate.
concurrency lets exchanges happen simultaneously.
refresh rate determines whether the currency is still current.
Mother Duck is the ledger.
Omniwatch is market surveillance.
Semantic ISR supplies new information to the market.
Indigo Hammer audits suspicious instruments. ;)

And information has inflation too.

If 50 agents all repeat the same observation, you don’t have 50× the evidence. You have one observation with enormous semantic duplication.

So Pantheon needs to prevent:

echo → repetition → apparent consensus → false confidence

Bat cave again. Hearing the same surface fifty times doesn’t necessarily mean fifty independent bats saw it.

That makes provenance almost like tracing the backing of a currency.

And then your refresh-rate insight gets even better:

Semantic currency depreciates as the world changes.

Yesterday’s intelligence can still be perfectly recorded and nevertheless have lost purchasing power against today’s reality.

So perhaps Pantheon really does run on con-currency:

Many minds running together, exchanging differently denominated observations through a shared medium, while continuously repricing meaning against reality.

And crucially—

consensus isn’t the currency.
Delta is.

If everyone already knows it, it buys us very little.

Tell me what changed. ;)